---
import { ArrowUpRight } from '@lucide/astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile, url } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About" active="About">
  <section class="shell page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">The person behind the projects</span><h1>A little about me<span>.</span></h1><p>I'm Victor, a technical lead with a background in civil engineering, mobility analytics, and data products.</p></section>
  <section class="shell about-layout"><div class="about-photo"><img src={url('images/victor-j-sequi-portrait.jpg')} alt="Victor J. Sequi" width="540" height="540" /><p>Technical leadership / Data / Applied AI</p></div><div class="prose"><h2>Understanding the problem comes first.</h2><p>I enjoy working out what people actually need, understanding their constraints, and turning that into a design a team can deliver. My work connects product needs, architecture, data contracts, implementation, and acceptance criteria.</p><p>At Vodafone, my current focus is data and reporting. Earlier work includes telecommunications analytics, reconciliation, and AI prototypes involving retrieval, tool-using agents, and evaluation.</p><p>Before that, I worked in transport and mobility analytics at AECOM, Citi Logik, and Amey. At Citi Logik, I was technical lead for an EV charge-point analysis and forecasting product, developing its methodology and PySpark pipeline.</p><h2>Building is how I keep learning.</h2><p>My direct programming experience centres on Python, PySpark, and SQL. I also direct, review, and validate agent-assisted development, including web applications and cloud infrastructure.</p><p>My independent projects give me room to explore the whole product: the problem, the data, the interface, and what it takes to operate it. This site is a place to make that work, and the thinking behind it, visible.</p><a class="text-link" href={profile.linkedin}>Connect on LinkedIn <ArrowUpRight size={18} aria-hidden="true" /></a></div></section>
  <section class="shell experience"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">The path so far</span><h2>A connected progression</h2></div></div><ol class="timeline"><li><span>2023 - present</span><div><h3>Vodafone</h3><p>Technical leadership across data, reporting, and earlier applied AI initiatives.</p></div></li><li><span>2022 - 2023</span><div><h3>Amey</h3><p>Data science and mobility insights from mobile-network data.</p></div></li><li><span>2021 - 2022</span><div><h3>Citi Logik</h3><p>Mobility data products, modelling, and EV charging analysis.</p></div></li><li><span>2016 - 2021</span><div><h3>AECOM</h3><p>Transport planning, demand modelling, and analytical automation.</p></div></li></ol></section>
</Base>
